# Checkmate in Time Line Fragment (4x4, two timelines), found with a search over the engine: White steps the king
# (d1 -> d2) on the white-moveable board (timeline 1), then Black plays pawn c4-c3 on timeline 0 and the bishop c4-d3 on
# timeline 1; White then has no legal turn and its king is attacked: "Black wins!" (Checkmate).
# Layout (1400x800): Versus (150,250); mode row 8 (690,604 after scrolling the list two notches); Play (808,712); Submit (841,90). Squares are clicked by name
# (`clicksq <timeline> <half-turn> <square>`), see game-standard.ui.
wait 20
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
move 690 400
wheel -2             # the list scrolls: the ninth row comes up to the eighth
wait 10
click 690 604        # Misc - Time Line Fragment (row 8)
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
capture endgame-start
clicksq 1 0 d1       # the white king
wait 40
clicksq 1 0 d2       # one step up
wait 40
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 90
capture endgame-black-to-move
clicksq 0 1 c4       # the black pawn on timeline 0
wait 40
clicksq 0 1 c3       # one step down
wait 60
capture endgame-black-first-move
clicksq 1 1 c4       # the black bishop on timeline 1
wait 40
clicksq 1 1 d3       # diagonal step
wait 90
capture endgame-black-second-move
click 841 90         # Submit: White has no legal turn
wait 150
capture endgame-end-card
